person('jackson_lears',
 'A cultural historian of the United States whose work connects religious longing, commercial persuasion and the making of meaning. In his written exchange with B. R. Cohen he explains cultural history as an inquiry into meanings formed through lived anxieties and desires, including unintended consequences. Advertising is examined through trust and confidence as well as sales. His conversation with David Serlin describes chance and control as intertwined practices rather than mutually exclusive eras, linking gambling, belief and economic life without claiming that calculation eliminates uncertainty.',
 'No Place of Grace (1981; Chicago reissue 1994 and later anniversary edition distinct); Fables of Abundance (1994; paperback 1995 distinct); Something for Nothing: Luck in America (2003).',
 [ev('lears_grace','No Place of Grace',1981,['cic_lears_1981'],'Existing metadata distinguishes Pantheon original 1981 from Chicago 1994 and the fortieth-anniversary edition. Book unread.'),ev('lears_fables','Fables of Abundance',1994,[sid('lears_serlin'),sid('lears_smithsonian')],'Contemporary author biography gives Basic Books 1994; Smithsonian confirms c1994. Later paperback date is not first publication.'),ev('lears_luck','Something for Nothing: Luck in America',2003,[sid('lears_serlin')],'Contemporary interview introduction and author biography give 2003, Viking Penguin. The June 2005 conversation is a separate fact.')],
 [rel('culture','Defines cultural history through historically situated meanings, conflicting desires and unintended consequences.',[sid('lears_cohen'),sid('lears_serlin')],'Author answers in the Cohen interview, section II; Serlin interview answers on overlapping chance/control. These are Lears’s stated interpretive methods, not certification of each example or a field-wide consensus.'),rel('consumption','Connects commercial persuasion to culturally specific practices of confidence, trust and uncertainty.',[sid('lears_cohen')],'Cohen interview, section I, where Lears discusses Fables of Abundance and the historical settings of confidence. The complete advertising monograph remains unread and no timeless national character is inferred.')],
 [source('lears_cohen','B. R. Cohen and T. J. Jackson Lears, “The Confidence Economy: An Interview with T. J. Jackson Lears,” Public Books, online written interview.','https://www.publicbooks.org/the-confidence-economy-an-interview-with-t-j-jackson-lears/','Written sections I–II read. Supports the author’s own account of confidence and cultural history. A reliable publication date was not established from the visible page, so none is invented and no chronology event is dated from crawl metadata. Other sections and complete book bodies not claimed read.',True),source('lears_serlin','David Serlin and Jackson Lears, “Rolling the Dice: An Interview with Jackson Lears,” Cabinet 19 (Fall 2005); conversation June 2005.','https://www.cabinetmagazine.org/issues/19/serlin_lears.php','Opening answers on the origins of the chance inquiry and the coexistence of chance/control read, plus introduction and author biography. Distinguishes June conversation from Fall issue. Contemporary bibliography gives Fables (1994) and Something for Nothing (2003); full books unread.',True),source('lears_smithsonian','Smithsonian Libraries and Archives, Fables of Abundance, record siris_sil_471135.','https://www.si.edu/object/siris_sil_471135','Author authority heading T. J. Jackson Lears 1947- and book date/copyright 1994 checked. Bibliographic facts only; open author date does not prove current living status.')],old=['cic_lears_1981'],scope='The author is the Rutgers historian also indexed as T. J. Jackson Lears; the matched title list grounds the identity. Existing No Place of Grace publisher-only qualification is unchanged. Two bounded author interviews support selected arguments; no full book reading, automatic McKay influence or broad political genealogy.',
 life_sources=[life('https://history.rutgers.edu/people/faculty/details/187-lears-tj-jackson','Rutgers History, T. J. Jackson Lears','Current emeritus listing and Raritan editorship','Positive present listing as Professor Emeritus and Editor-in-Chief; page distinguishes service 1986–2025.'),life('https://www.si.edu/object/siris_sil_471135','Smithsonian, Fables of Abundance','Author heading','Birth year 1947; open end not living evidence.','Institutional library heading checked.')],birth=1947)
person('antoine_prost',
 'A French historian of education, social life and the aftermath of war who also examines historical knowledge and practice. Maurice Agulhon’s substantive reading describes the veterans study as joining organization, social composition and commemorative practices, while challenging an automatic identification of veterans with fascism. Agulhon also questions whether that correction goes too far. Danièle Voldman reads Douze leçons as both a methodological exposition and a situated defence of historical understanding. These readings support the entry without claiming that the underlying books have been read in full.',
 'Histoire de l’enseignement en France, 1800–1967 (1968); Les Anciens Combattants et la société française, 1914–1939 (three volumes, 1977; with collaboration of Philippe Billois); Douze leçons sur l’histoire (1996).',
 [ev('prost_enseignement','Histoire de l’enseignement en France, 1800–1967',1968,[sid('prost_education')],'Author’s later publisher-hosted preface bibliography gives Armand Colin 1968. Book body unread.'),ev('prost_combattants','Les Anciens Combattants et la société française: three-volume publication',1977,[sid('prost_combattants')],'Institutional catalogue records 1977 and three volumes Histoire; Sociologie; Mentalités et idéologies, with Philippe Billois as collaborator. Not a thesis-defense date or the separate shorter Gallimard book.'),ev('prost_lecons','Douze leçons sur l’histoire',1996,[sid('prost_voldman')],'Contemporary review records Seuil 1996, 330 pages. The 2014 edition is not substituted for original publication.')],
 [rel('memory','Integrates veterans’ organizations and commemorative practices into a social history of postwar France.',[sid('prost_agulhon')],'Agulhon 1979, pp. 831–832, read: specifically discusses November 11 ceremonies, monuments and village sociability. His account of Prost’s political correction includes reservations about its extent. No uncritical consensus or whole-book reading.'),rel('philhistory','Makes methods, question formation and the historian’s social position explicit problems of historical knowledge.',[sid('prost_voldman')],'Voldman’s substantive 1996 review, pp. 174–175, attributes this methodological and epistemological argument to Douze leçons. The book itself remains unread; this is not an inferred connection from its title alone.')],
 [source('prost_education','Antoine Prost, Histoire de l’enseignement en France, 1800–1967 (Paris: Armand Colin, 1968): bibliographic witness in the author’s later preface.','https://catalogue-editions.ens-lyon.fr/resources/titles/29021100698980/extras/Pr_face_d_Antoine_Prost.pdf','Publisher-hosted primary preface, bibliography note 16 on printed p. 17, checked for author/title/Armand Colin 1968 and 525-page description. Preface body and the 1968 book not read for substantive claims.'),source('prost_combattants','Antoine Prost, avec la collaboration de Philippe Billois, Les Anciens Combattants et la société française, 1914–1939 (Paris: Presses de la Fondation nationale des sciences politiques, 1977), three volumes.','https://patrimoine.bm-grenoble.fr/PATRIMOINE/doc/SYRACUSE/502267/les-anciens-combattants-et-la-societe-francaise-1914-1939-de-antoine-prost','Grenoble institutional catalogue checked for full three-volume credit, 1977 and the collaborator Philippe Billois. Publisher volume-2 record https://www.pressesdesciencespo.fr/fr/book/?GCOI=27246100664730 corroborates first publication in 1977; its English-original-language and modern ebook day/month fields are not adopted. Neither the original study nor its shorter Gallimard counterpart read.'),source('prost_agulhon','Maurice Agulhon, review of Antoine Prost, Les Anciens Combattants et la société française, Annales E.S.C. 34:4 (1979): 831–833.','https://www.persee.fr/doc/ahess_0395-2649_1979_num_34_4_294088_t1_0831_0000_001','Printed pp. 831–832 read through Persée text, including organization/sociology/mentalities, monuments and ceremonies, and the qualified challenge to equating veterans with the far right. P. 833 unread. Substantive book claims remain explicitly mediated by Agulhon; his reservations are retained.',True),source('prost_voldman','Danièle Voldman, review of Antoine Prost, Douze leçons sur l’histoire, Vingtième Siècle 52 (October–December 1996): 174–175.','https://www.persee.fr/doc/xxs_0294-1759_1996_num_52_1_3587_t1_0174_0000_1','Review text on printed pp. 174–175 read through Persée: methodological exposition, social position/question formation, and defence of understanding rather than reliving the past. Review citation confirms Seuil 1996, 330 pages. Prost’s book remains unread; interpretation is attributed to Voldman.',True)],scope='New identity is the French historian of education and veterans, distinguished from other Prost authors by matching institutional and publication records. Argument claims use named substantive readers Agulhon and Voldman. Book bodies remain unread. Billois’s collaboration, the three-volume format, original publication years and separate shorter/late editions stay explicit. No generic university, political-affiliation or influence arrows.',
 life_sources=[life('https://www.editionsdelasorbonne.fr/auteur/968/antoine-prost','Éditions de la Sorbonne, Antoine Prost','Current author biography','Positive institutional author listing as professor emeritus, identifying the education historian.'),life('https://www.lemonde.fr/signataires/antoine-prost/','Antoine Prost, signed contributions in Le Monde','Signed tribune, published 11 July 2025','Positive recent author activity; this is a signed opinion article, not an interview. No substantive retirement-policy claim used.','Byline and publication date checked; no inference from unrelated sidebar dates.'),life('https://patrimoine.bm-grenoble.fr/PATRIMOINE/doc/SYRACUSE/502267/les-anciens-combattants-et-la-societe-francaise-1914-1939-de-antoine-prost','Grenoble library, Les Anciens Combattants','Author heading','Birth year 1933; open end is not living evidence.','Institutional bibliographic heading checked.')],birth=1933,life_limit='Living inference combines a present institutional biography with a signed July 2025 publication; no unsupported exact birth day is asserted.')

